1
00:00:02,407 --> 00:00:05,844
(Qexample) OFFICER: Good morning. What can I do for you?

2
00:00:05,844 --> 00:00:11,817
LOUISE: I want to report a theft. I had some things stolen out of my bag yesterday.&nbsp;

3
00:00:11,817 --> 00:00:19,864
OFFICER: I'm sorry to hear that. Right, so I'll need to take a few details. Can I start with your name?

4
00:00:19,864 --> 00:00:22,745
LOUISE: Louise Taylor.&nbsp;

5
00:00:22,745 --> 00:00:27,297
(Q1) [resident = nationality 解释] OFFICER: OK, thank you. And are you resident in the UK?

6
00:00:27,297 --> 00:00:32,795
[Q1答案句] LOUISE: No, I'm actually Canadian, though my mother was British.&nbsp;

7
00:00:32,795 --> 00:00:35,081
OFFICER: And your date of birth?

8
00:00:35,081 --> 00:00:39,442
LOUISE: December 14th, 1977.&nbsp;

9
00:00:39,442 --> 00:00:42,944
(Q2) OFFICER: So you're just visiting this country?

10
00:00:42,944 --> 00:00:52,777
[Q2答案句] LOUISE: That's right. I come over most summers on business. I'm an interior designer and I come over to buy old furniture, antiques you know.&nbsp;

11
00:00:52,777 --> 00:01:02,764
There are some really lovely things around here, but you need to get out to the small towns. I've had a really good trip this year, until this happened.

12
00:01:02,764 --> 00:01:06,894
(Q3) OFFICER: OK. So you've been here quite a while?

13
00:01:06,894 --> 00:01:11,933
LOUISE: Yes, I'm here for two months. I go back next week.&nbsp;

14
00:01:11,933 --> 00:01:15,977
[Q3定位词： stay = address 解释， now=current 近义词] OFFICER: So may I ask where you're staying now?

15
00:01:15,977 --> 00:01:22,878
[Q3答案句：at present = current] LOUISE: Well at present I've got a place at Park Apartments, that's on King Street.&nbsp;

16
00:01:22,878 --> 00:01:32,677
[Q3干扰项] I was staying at the Riverside Apartments on the same street, but the apartment there was only available for six weeks so I had to find another one.

17
00:01:32,677 --> 00:01:36,063
OFFICER: OK. And the apartment number?

18
00:01:36,063 --> 00:01:38,313
LOUISE: Fifteen.&nbsp;

19
00:01:38,313 --> 00:01:40,024
OFFICER: Right.

20
00:01:40,024 --> 00:01:48,712
(Q4) OFFICER: Now, I need to take some details of the theft. So you said you had some things stolen out of your bag?

21
00:01:48,712 --> 00:01:50,965
LOUISE: That's right.&nbsp;

22
00:01:50,965 --> 00:01:57,159
OFFICER: And were you actually carrying the bag when the theft took place?

23
00:01:57,159 --> 00:02:09,836
Yes. I really can't understand it. I had my backpack on. And I went into a supermarket to buy a few things and when I opened it up my wallet wasn't there.&nbsp;

24
00:02:09,836 --> 00:02:31,676
[Q4答案句] OFFICER: And what did your wallet have in it?LOUISE: Well, fortunately I don't keep my credit cards in that wallet - I keep them with my passport in an inside compartment in my backpack.&nbsp; &nbsp;But there was quite a bit of cash there…about ￡250 sterling, I should think.

25
00:02:31,676 --> 00:02:42,669
(Q5) I withdrew ￡300 from my account yesterday, but I did a bit of shopping, so I must have already spent about ￡50 of that.

26
00:02:42,669 --> 00:02:45,186
OFFICER: OK.

27
00:02:45,186 --> 00:02:54,304
[Q5答案句] LOUISE: At first I thought, oh I must have left the wallet back in the apartment, but then I realised my phone had gone as well.&nbsp;

28
00:02:54,304 --> 00:03:04,716
It was only a week old, and that's when I realised I'd been robbed. Anyway at least they didn't take the keys to my rental car.

29
00:03:04,716 --> 00:03:15,497
(Q6) [Q6答案句] OFFICER: Yes. So you say the theft occurred yesterday?LOUISE: Yes.&nbsp;OFFICER: So that was September the tenth.

30
00:03:15,497 --> 00:03:22,800
(Q7) [where= location] And do you have any idea at all of where or when the things might possibly have been stolen?

31
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:31,596
LOUISE: Well at first I couldn't believe it because the bag had been on my back ever since I left the apartment after lunch.

32
00:03:31,596 --> 00:03:39,478
It's just a small backpack, but I generally use it when I'm travelling because it seems safer than a handbag.

33
00:03:39,478 --> 00:03:46,686
[Q7答案句： 但 4pm后面才出现【答案前置】] Anyway, I met up with a friend, and we spent a couple of hours in the museum.

34
00:03:46,686 --> 00:03:52,003
(Q8) But I do remember that as we were leaving there, at about 4 o'clock,

35
00:03:52,003 --> 00:04:04,585
[Q8答案句] a group of young boys ran up to us, and they were really crowding round us, and they were asking us what time it was, then all of a sudden they ran off.

36
00:04:04,585 --> 00:04:07,883
(Q9) OFFICER: Can you remember anything about them?

37
00:04:07,883 --> 00:04:19,752
LOUISE: The one who did most of the talking was wearing a T-shirt with a picture of something…let's see… a tiger.&nbsp;

38
00:04:19,752 --> 00:04:23,865
OFFICER: Right. Any idea of how old he might have been?

39
00:04:23,865 --> 00:04:27,365
LOUISE: Around twelve years old?&nbsp;

40
00:04:27,365 --> 00:04:32,230
OFFICER: And can you remember anything else about his appearance?

41
00:04:32,230 --> 00:04:37,127
LOUISE: Not much. He was quite thin…&nbsp;

42
00:04:37,127 --> 00:04:45,947
[Q9答案句] OFFICER: Colour of hair?LOUISE: I do remember that - he was blond. All the others were dark-haired.&nbsp;

43
00:04:45,947 --> 00:04:49,478
OFFICER: And any details of the others?

44
00:04:49,478 --> 00:04:54,947
LOUISE: Not really. They came and went so quickly.&nbsp;

45
00:04:54,947 --> 00:05:15,504
(Q10) [Q10答案句] OFFICER: Right. So what I'm going to do now is give you a crime reference number so you can contact your insurance company.So this is ten digits: 87954 82361

46
00:05:15,504 --> 00:05:18,004
LOUISE: Thank you. So should I …&nbsp;

